<html>
<title>Other Configurations</title>
<body>

<h1>Other Configurations</h1>

<p>
The Other sub-tab shows I/O configuration and status for additional hardware components of the emulated computer. The Other sub-tab interface is shown below:
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/configuration_other.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<p>
To open this tab, select the <strong>Configuration</strong> tab (1) and then the <strong>Other</strong> sub-tab (2).
</p>


<h2>I/O</h2>

<p>
The I/O section displays register values and allows toggling individual I/O functions. The I/O controls are shown in the screenshot below.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/configuration_other_io.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>HW or chip</strong> field - the configured other HW chip.</li>
<li>(2) <strong>I/O</strong> field - shows I/O values and configuration.</li>
</ul>

<p>
Depending on the HW chip, the I/O definition may include the following headings:
</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Function</strong> - description of the I/O function.</li>
<li><strong>D</strong> - <strong>D</strong>irection (I = input, O = output, B = both). B is not used in the screenshot example.</li>
<li><strong>P</strong> - <strong>P</strong>ort number.</li>
<li><strong>Value</strong> - current register value.</li>
</ul>

<p>
The following hardware configurations are currently supported:
</p>

<ul>
<li>CT Payphone</li>
</ul>

<p>
Only I/O information and controls are shown for configured hardware chips.
</p>


<h2>Log</h2>

<p>
The Log section controls logging of I/O events. The Log controls are shown in the screenshot below.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/configuration_other_log.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>Log</strong> button - switch log on/off (default off).</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Time</strong> button - switch time logging on/off (default on).</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Clear</strong> button - clear log window.</li>
<li>(4) <strong>I/O</strong> checkbox - enable or disable logging for individual I/O functions.</li>
</ul>

</body>
</html>


